      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, here's a quick comparison table for you:\n\n| Factor              | ETFs (Exchange-Traded Funds)                                                    | Mutual Funds                                                                   |\n|---------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Liquidity**       | Higher liquidity: Can be bought and sold throughout the trading day on a stock exchange. | Lower liquidity: Can only be bought or sold at the end of the trading day at the net asset value (NAV). |\n| **Management**      | Active: Traded by the end of the day, with a value that changes throughout the day. Passive: Heavy reliance on index tracking.                     | Mutual funds can either be actively managed (fund managers make decisions) or passively managed (tracking an index). Active management tends to result in higher fees, while passive management often leads to lower fees. |\n\nI hope this helps with your memo!",
